## Project Structure

```
src/{{ package_name }}/
  agents/                   # Agent definitions
    example.py              # Example agent ({{ agent_framework }})
  tools/                    # Agent tools/functions
{%- if execution_model == "cli" %}
  cli.py                    # Typer CLI entry point
  commands/                 # CLI subcommands
{%- else %}
  app.py                    # FastAPI app factory
{%- if enable_otel %}
  telemetry.py              # OpenTelemetry setup
{%- endif %}
  routers/                  # HTTP endpoint definitions
    health.py               # /healthz, /readyz
  controllers/              # Request orchestration
  dtos/                     # Pydantic request/response models
{%- endif %}
{%- if execution_model == "web" %}
  web/                      # Frontend integration
    serve.py                # Static file serving for production
    frontend/               # Frontend application (scaffolded separately)
{%- endif %}
  config.py                 # Pydantic-settings based config
  logging.py                # structlog setup
  services/                 # Business logic
{%- if include_clients %}
  clients/                  # External API/service clients
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
  db.py                     # Async engine/session setup
  models/                   # SQLAlchemy models
  repositories/             # Data access layer
{%- endif %}
tests/
  unit/                     # Unit tests
  integration/              # Integration tests
  e2e/                      # End-to-end tests
```

## Key Conventions

- Source code lives in `src/{{ package_name }}/` (src layout).
- **Agents** live in `agents/`. Tools the agent can call go in `tools/`.
{%- if execution_model == "cli" %}
- **Commands** are thin I/O wrappers. Parse CLI args, call the agent, format output.
{%- else %}
- **Layering:** routers -> controllers -> services (agents live in services layer).
- **DTOs** are Pydantic models for API I/O, always separate from DB models.
{%- endif %}
- Tests are organized by type in `tests/unit/`, `tests/integration/`, `tests/e2e/`.
- Use `@pytest.mark.external` for tests that hit external services.
- All config is in `pyproject.toml` — no separate config files.
{%- if execution_model == "cli" %}
- Version is defined in `pyproject.toml` and read via `importlib.metadata`.
{%- elif execution_model == "web" %}
- Backend: `just dev-be`. Frontend: `just dev-fe`. Both: `just dev`.
{%- else %}
- Run locally with `uv run uvicorn {{ package_name }}.app:app --reload`.
{%- endif %}

